# Home: bring the target's arms to the program's start, through the twin (ADR-0071,
# ADR-0072: the target names which sides - the simulation, the real arm, or both).
#
# `cite_bringup.program.cycle.home`, the sequence `./scripts/home` runs: initialize
# every physical arm the target commands, measure the start on every side of the
# target, and only where one is not there move the target's arms there with one
# signal, in the target's twin mode; then measure again. Nothing is retried. Where
# the target commands a physical side the console first reads the twin's mode as
# SIM, waits for the physical carriage to be reported stationary and asks the
# operator to clear the cell (ConfirmOperator), and puts the twin back in SIM
# afterwards. The run holds the twin's mode for its whole length (HoldMode.srv).
# Rejected unless Start robot has succeeded and the console is READY. Cancelling
# the goal is the same software stop as StopCell. A success marks every side of the
# target at the start (ConsoleState.plant_at_start / counterpart_at_start).
#
# Served under the plan's `console.home` (ConsoleState.msg).

float64 speed_scale     # (0, 1] of the program's own speed, sent explicitly by
                        # the operator's panel. Never defaulted: a goal with 0, or
                        # any value outside (0, 1] or below
                        # ConsoleState.minimum_speed_scale, is rejected (ADR-0071
                        # decision 2). The floor applies only to a target in
                        # ConsoleState.floored_targets
uint8 target            # ConsoleState.TARGET_SIM, TARGET_REAL or TARGET_TWIN, sent
                        # explicitly by the operator's panel (ADR-0072). Never
                        # defaulted: 0, an unknown value, or a target not in
                        # ConsoleState.available_targets is rejected
---
bool success
string detail           # what was done, or which step failed and why
---
string step             # the step being done now, as the operator reads it
